  "unit": "Unit 6 - Manipulating & Solving Equations",
  "description": "Comprehensive lesson covering Unit 6 - Manipulating & Solving Equations for SAT Math preparation.",
  "duration": 45,
  "content": "<ol>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Cancelling incorrectly</strong><br />\n   - Wrong: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></math><br />\n   - Correct: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></math>  </p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Losing solutions when multiplying/dividing by a variable</strong><br />\n   - If you multiply or divide by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>, always check <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02260;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>.  </p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Forgetting to distribute negatives</strong><br />\n   - <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>, not <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>  </p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Square root mistake</strong><br />\n   - <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo></mrow></math>, not <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>  </p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<hr />\n\n<h3>Inverse operations</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Addition ↔ Subtraction  </li>\n<li>Multiplication ↔ Division  </li>\n<li>Squaring ↔ Square root  </li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong><br />\nSolve <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow></math>  </p>\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>9</mn><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>\n\n<h3>Balancing equations</h3>\n<p>What you do to one side, do to the other.</p>\n<hr />\n\n<h3>Distribute and Combine</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Expand parentheses and combine like terms.  </li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong><br />\nSolve <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></math>  </p>\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>12</mn><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>12</mn><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>\n\n<h3>Fractions</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Multiply through by least common denominator (LCD).  </li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong><br />\nSolve <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math><br />\nMultiply both sides by 15:  </p>\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>15</mn><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>\n\n<h3>Decimals</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Multiply through by powers of 10 to clear decimals.  </li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong><br />\nSolve <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>0.2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1.3</mn></mrow></math><br />\nMultiply through by 10:  </p>\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>13</mn><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math>\n\n<hr />\n\n<ul>\n<li>Always simplify before solving.  </li>\n<li>Eliminate fractions and decimals early.  </li>\n<li>Plug solution back to check (some SAT questions have “extraneous solutions”).  </li>\n<li>Watch for absolute values, square roots, and restrictions.  </li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n\n<p>1) Solve: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>18</mn></mrow></math><br />\n2) Solve: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></math><br />\n3) Solve: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></math><br />\n4) Solve: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>0.2</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow></math><br />\n5) Simplify: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></math>  </p>\n<hr />\n\n<p>1) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></math><br />\n2) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></math><br />\n3) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math><br />\n4) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0.3</mn><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math><br />\n5) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></math> (for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02260;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>)</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-python\">\n</code></pre>",
